WEBVTT

00:09.530 --> 00:17.530
During a business lunch with Obama, the Secret Service notices something odd. The
mysterious message “I'll be waiting in Nakaetsu Village <3” is written on his forehead.

00:18.040 --> 00:24.299
Deciding they mustn't make the village chief wait, they take a private
jet, but must have been somehow mistaken as they arrive at a tent city.

00:24.300 --> 00:27.089
Isn't that dramatic?

00:27.090 --> 00:30.579
The deeply dramatic inhabitants hold a heartwarming
welcoming party, their voices forming a chorus.

00:30.580 --> 00:34.169
No! To the treaty! No! To the treaty!
Others are mixed in.

00:34.170 --> 00:35.649
Wait, what era is this!?

00:35.650 --> 00:37.409
A time slip has occured.

00:37.410 --> 00:39.579
Fathers are chic leftists, while
sons post fascist rants online.

00:39.580 --> 00:41.419
A generation gap has occured as well.

00:41.420 --> 00:47.919
Looking all unconcerned and going “You're non-political, right?”, “You're non-political,
right?”, a group of activists resembling Asashoryu forced me into joining them.

00:47.920 --> 00:52.539
As their numbers swelled to over twenty, they made
their way to the demonstration site, an SDF garrison.

00:52.540 --> 00:57.119
Due to the previous generation gap, with a clap of
thunder they fell through a time slip to the Sengoku era.

00:57.120 --> 01:00.939
Thus, we became Sengoku demonstraters,
and were attacked by Naoe's forces.

01:00.940 --> 01:05.199
Entertainingly peppered with arrows, we
were momentarily wiped out. Except for me.

01:05.200 --> 01:13.200
Prostrating myself and begging for my life, a man with “love” on his helmet
took an interest in my perfect form, and gave me a helmet with “hole” on it.

01:15.870 --> 01:17.369
I wasn't very impressed.

01:17.370 --> 01:25.370
Give me a helmet of love too, I shouted,
and accidentally decapitated Naoe himself.

01:26.070 --> 01:30.020
At that moment, history changed.

01:30.860 --> 01:32.530
- Mr. Kumeta Koji Mr. MAEDAX.R, for lending us your portrait and your white briefs, 　thank you.
- Mr. Hata Kenjiro for your work as a voice actor and photographs with other voice actors, 　thank you.

01:30.860 --> 01:32.740
Kodansha,
for a miraculous second OAD,
thank you.

01:33.480 --> 01:35.190
- King Records, We will never forget your face when you heard the sales numbers for the <i>Sayonara, Zetsubou-sensei</i> DVDs. 　Thank you.
- Mr. Ohtsuki Kenji, For all the viewers who tuned in to hear the OP and were too lazy to change the channel away, thank you.

01:36.110 --> 01:37.860
- Mr. Kamiya Hiroshi, for saying “SHAFT can't be helped”, thank you.
- Our new fans, for saying “I stopped on it while channel-surfing”, thank you.

01:36.110 --> 01:37.860
- Our old fans, for saying “season one was better”, thank you.
- Those who bought the DVDs, for saying “where's S4?”, thank you.

01:36.110 --> 01:37.860
ff

01:38.860 --> 01:40.580
- Nozomu is worn out and can't run anymore. Please forgive us.
- He could have kept going in Kyoto.

02:23.280 --> 02:23.410
- YOU
- TOO

