04:56.510 --> 04:57.790
Automated External Defibrillator

05:00.820 --> 05:04.350
- Thought I was lucky finding a chocolate-covered
marshmallow - But it was really a bug

05:00.820 --> 05:04.369
All right, let's explain how to use an AED.

05:04.351 --> 05:05.351
One

05:05.460 --> 05:09.749
If you notice someone who's collapsed
and isn't breathing, bring the AED to them.

05:09.030 --> 05:09.750
- ※ Call an ambulance at the same time
- ※ Call an ambulance at the same time

05:09.750 --> 05:10.750
Two

05:10.621 --> 05:13.969
Second, place the pads
on the chest as instructed by the handbook.

05:13.950 --> 05:14.950
Three

05:14.971 --> 05:19.440
Third, step back from the collapsed person
and press the button to administer the shock.

05:20.000 --> 05:23.900
Isn't the AED a wonderful device?

05:26.000 --> 05:31.199
You should all study its proper use in case
of emergencies.

05:26.010 --> 05:28.325
The noises coming from next door

05:28.326 --> 05:30.639
are always R&$ident Evil

05:30.640 --> 05:32.160
When it changed, it was Monster H♪♪ter

05:31.200 --> 05:32.200
Sorry!

05:34.380 --> 05:39.849
Wait, why are we starting off
with something useful, rather than a gag?

05:39.850 --> 05:46.899
Come on, if I don't do this, mumble-mumble will probably
be angry at me for causing misconceptions about AEDs.

05:46.900 --> 05:49.049
Now, on to the main topic.

05:49.050 --> 05:49.950
Human lives are one thing,

05:49.951 --> 05:54.769
but in this world there are many
things that should never be resuscitated!

05:54.770 --> 05:56.889
Sometimes, we must be sure not to use...

05:56.890 --> 05:58.920
The dysfunctional AED!

06:00.850 --> 06:02.489
Dysfunctional... AED.

06:02.490 --> 06:03.490
Abbreviated––

06:04.810 --> 06:08.159
What a shame, it would
have made the joke far better as DEAD.

06:08.160 --> 06:10.549
There's nothing wrong with avoiding that!

06:10.550 --> 06:12.219
Yes... In this world...

06:12.220 --> 06:15.449
so many things are
being kept alive by DAEDs!

06:15.450 --> 06:17.499
To hold together a falling dictatorship,

06:17.500 --> 06:18.989
they fire the missiles!

06:18.990 --> 06:21.379
To stimulate the dead Japanese economy,

06:21.380 --> 06:23.229
they make the highway tolls 1000 yen!

06:23.230 --> 06:24.649
To freshen up idols who are fading fast,

06:24.650 --> 06:26.499
they keep things going by stripping!

06:26.500 --> 06:28.649
These are the kinds of DAED we have.

06:28.650 --> 06:32.660
We still must save every life we can!

06:30.110 --> 06:32.660
Hyper Media　 Creator

06:36.040 --> 06:38.960
Ohkusa's maternal
insticts are running wild!

06:38.960 --> 06:40.420
Night Watch Room

06:43.990 --> 06:46.340
It's all over...

06:47.070 --> 06:49.009
What's over, Komori!?

06:49.010 --> 06:54.889
Teacher just
isn't interested in me anymore.

06:54.890 --> 06:56.969
It must be the seven-year itch!

06:56.970 --> 06:58.170
I'll revive your relationship!

07:00.660 --> 07:02.030
What have you done!?

07:04.840 --> 07:08.440
Time for your injection, Mr. Itoshiki.

07:09.930 --> 07:11.649
What's that supposed to mean?

07:11.650 --> 07:12.650
Oh, nothing.

07:13.030 --> 07:17.329
See, this is something couples always do
when they start to get bored of each other.

07:17.330 --> 07:20.790
She dresses up like a nurse
in the hope that it will light a spark.

07:21.370 --> 07:23.559
Go ahead, act like you're still young.

07:23.560 --> 07:25.750
What do you mean, “still young”!?

07:26.000 --> 07:27.160
Normally...

07:31.560 --> 07:33.739
We wear our sailor uniforms.

07:33.550 --> 07:34.790
※ Edit: Check this

07:33.740 --> 07:36.029
For us, those are normal.

07:36.030 --> 07:41.309
I can't get bored when I wasn't interested
in any of you in the first place!

07:41.310 --> 07:43.810
Wait, what's this supposed to be!?

07:46.280 --> 07:48.940
Who switched the clothes in my locker!?

07:47.606 --> 07:48.940
Staff Lockers

07:50.100 --> 07:52.450
See, now he's acting like a schoolboy!

07:53.110 --> 07:54.110
That's lame.

07:56.090 --> 07:58.869
MILFs in sailor uniforms are lame.

07:58.870 --> 08:00.609
Who are you calling a MILF!?

08:00.610 --> 08:01.850
The only MILF in the room, duh.

08:03.030 --> 08:06.199
I must save the others, too!

08:06.200 --> 08:07.400
Hold it!

08:09.130 --> 08:12.070
I can't even pull off a comb-over anymore.

08:12.640 --> 08:16.149
Don't worry! I'll give
you a perm and then no one will notice!

08:16.150 --> 08:17.430
I guess that'll work.

08:21.560 --> 08:24.000
Boys' Room

08:21.790 --> 08:25.169
There, I prolonged
its life! Now no one can tell!

08:25.170 --> 08:26.440
Are you sure!?

08:27.900 --> 08:29.530
- Shinko Books
- Books

08:29.780 --> 08:33.599
The classics just aren't selling anymore.

08:33.600 --> 08:34.600
It's okay.

08:36.070 --> 08:39.559
This should bring its sales back up again!

08:38.580 --> 08:39.580
Bocchan

08:39.560 --> 08:42.869
Swap the labels on the sashimi at the
supermarket, and its shelf-life is extended!

08:42.870 --> 08:47.739
The books someone couldn't even get 10 yen for and just left to
be thrown out can be sold for 100 yen if you shave down the edges!

08:47.740 --> 08:51.180
Abandoned theme parks attract more
visitors than when they were in operation!

08:53.810 --> 08:58.260
Extending
life or being revived is a great thing!

08:59.720 --> 09:04.409
Oh no! Ohkusa is reviving everything
she can find in town!

09:04.410 --> 09:06.190
What do we do!?

09:31.420 --> 09:33.149
I told you this would happen!

09:33.150 --> 09:36.489
Now they're rising from their graves!

09:36.490 --> 09:38.899
The dead who should be left dead!

09:38.900 --> 09:42.389
The '80s shoulderpad suit zombie!

09:42.390 --> 09:45.400
And the frozen road construction zombie!

09:45.560 --> 09:47.970
If you get bitten, you'll be a zombie too!

09:48.170 --> 09:50.520
I don't wanna wear
a suit with shoulder pads!

09:50.960 --> 09:52.099
News flash!

09:52.100 --> 09:55.269
Stone-wash jeans
have come back in Harajuku!

09:55.270 --> 09:57.939
Is that the work of the zombies!?

09:57.940 --> 10:03.549
Routes 317, 311, 318,
and 246 are all infected!

10:03.550 --> 10:07.050
With public works projects revived, traffic
is at a standstill!

10:07.300 --> 10:09.239
The capital is in a panic!

10:09.240 --> 10:10.550
This is a pandemic!

10:10.720 --> 10:15.579
This is what happens when you keep things
alive that should have been allowed to die!

10:15.580 --> 10:18.759
What's
with this despair-inducing timeline!?

10:16.800 --> 10:18.230
AAAAA

10:18.760 --> 10:21.490
Teacher, the zombies are already here!

10:22.350 --> 10:24.850
Let's hide in that supermarket!

10:26.560 --> 10:29.809
Why has it come to this?

10:29.810 --> 10:32.569
We're doomed! This is the end of the world!

10:32.570 --> 10:35.070
Everyone's dead! No, they're undead!

10:42.830 --> 10:44.790
To be continued

10:46.580 --> 10:47.819
That's good.

10:47.820 --> 10:49.290
Excellent.

10:49.500 --> 10:51.459
What's so good about this!?

10:51.460 --> 10:54.170
Since you were bitten, your
life will be extended in serialization.

10:54.420 --> 10:57.800
Zombie serialization
where you'll never quite end.

10:58.100 --> 11:02.900
If you bite the readers, they'll become
zombie readers who will never stop.

11:04.020 --> 11:08.640
This kind of overserialization
has become pandemic in comics.

11:08.920 --> 11:12.209
I think we
should tear it down and build anew.

11:12.210 --> 11:15.750
But look how good the upper floors are.
Can't we keep it standing a little longer?

11:15.750 --> 11:16.320
No Man's Land 1

11:18.250 --> 11:20.990
It's no good. The foundation is rotten.

11:45.780 --> 11:48.990
I didn't expect the
tide to carry me this far...

11:48.990 --> 11:49.150
Missed ADR again

11:49.150 --> 11:49.320
Re-recutting

11:49.310 --> 11:49.490
Re-redubbing

11:49.490 --> 11:49.650
Push back release date

11:49.650 --> 11:50.060
Push back streaming

11:49.810 --> 11:50.060
Push back release date again

11:50.270 --> 11:52.130
