11:50.270 --> 11:53.990
Casting God Away

11:52.131 --> 11:53.990
From Chapter 193

11:57.060 --> 11:58.070
- Harima Park
- Tide Pool

12:00.260 --> 12:03.030
Isn't it strange to call it a tide pool?

12:01.531 --> 12:03.030
Please clean up your trash

12:05.770 --> 12:08.809
Isn't it more like
a pool where you get washed away?

12:08.810 --> 12:11.010
Well... I guess.

12:13.760 --> 12:16.480
Do you want to just get washed away!?

12:21.690 --> 12:23.459
Is something wrong?

12:23.460 --> 12:24.700
The heat's just getting to him.

12:24.630 --> 12:24.718
Ponyo

12:25.460 --> 12:27.470
I bought the Ponyo DVD!

12:27.680 --> 12:29.180
Me too!

12:29.390 --> 12:30.690
I did too!

12:30.690 --> 12:31.300
Noriko is Ponyo!

12:31.300 --> 12:33.060
I bought it too!

12:31.310 --> 12:33.310
Ponyo

12:34.970 --> 12:36.670
See, you're all being washed away.

12:39.360 --> 12:40.360
Hetaly

12:40.370 --> 12:43.240
when wet!

12:40.370 --> 12:43.240
Can they get away with this!? How shocking!

12:41.806 --> 12:43.240
Slippery

12:43.450 --> 12:45.360
- Slippery
- when wet!

12:43.450 --> 12:45.360
Do not run by pool

12:43.450 --> 12:45.320
That's not shocking at all.

12:45.570 --> 12:47.209
It's just normal.

12:47.210 --> 12:50.950
Oh really? Then maybe I
should pencil a little something in...

12:51.080 --> 12:51.118
Hetaly

12:52.080 --> 12:54.499
And she's swept away.

12:54.500 --> 12:56.550
With her annoying friends.

12:56.560 --> 12:56.670
- A - Help the
economic recovery - Buy DVDs this month

12:57.190 --> 12:58.519
I'm sorry.

12:57.713 --> 12:58.835
Do not...

12:58.520 --> 12:59.960
I can't have pets at my place.

12:58.836 --> 12:59.960
run...

13:00.190 --> 13:01.490
-  Story
-  Kitten

13:04.260 --> 13:07.130
But I want you so badly!

13:09.830 --> 13:12.600
Swept away by circumstances.

13:13.350 --> 13:17.269
Japanese have
always, as a race, easily been swept away.

13:17.270 --> 13:20.680
Put them in the right
pool, and there they go.

13:20.920 --> 13:25.700
Washed away by the class they transfer
into, they suddenly become Hanshin fans!

13:25.900 --> 13:29.830
If their acquaintances are annoying enough
about it, washed away at the ballot box!

13:26.570 --> 13:27.569
Vote for him

13:27.570 --> 13:28.819
Vote for him

13:28.820 --> 13:29.830
If you don't, I'll XXX

13:30.050 --> 13:35.159
Washed away by trends in the world (the
west), they change Japan's laws one by one!

13:35.160 --> 13:39.259
The youth of Japan are
forgetting their roots and washing away!

13:39.260 --> 13:40.560
Teacher!

13:43.030 --> 13:44.919
Oh, you're Miss Kitsu's sister.

13:44.920 --> 13:48.050
I'm glad we could meet again.

13:50.740 --> 13:52.410
Me too.

13:51.470 --> 13:52.430
- Volume 12
- aaaaaaaaa

13:53.540 --> 13:54.540
Eh!?

13:54.210 --> 13:55.430
New York!?

14:02.350 --> 14:06.490
Oh no! Teacher
has been swept away by the mood!

14:09.620 --> 14:12.439
I didn't expect the
tide to carry me this far.

14:12.440 --> 14:14.700
Wait, just where is this?

14:16.900 --> 14:19.589
“The tide carrying you here” is a strange
way to put it.

14:19.590 --> 14:20.480
After all, this is...

14:20.481 --> 14:22.361
The Island of
Those Who Don't Go With the Flow!

14:22.500 --> 14:23.729
You were there?

14:23.730 --> 14:25.049
Yes, always.

14:25.050 --> 14:28.669
The Island of Those Who Don't Go With
the Flow? What's that supposed to mean?

14:28.670 --> 14:33.050
It's where people who keep doing their own thing,
ignoring the influence of those around them, end up.

14:33.230 --> 14:35.250
It's like another Galapagos!

14:36.720 --> 14:38.220
There's one already!

14:42.990 --> 14:47.039
One who's ignored
the latest trends, and found his own style!

14:47.040 --> 14:49.570
It seems almost like I've seen one of
those somewhere!

14:53.200 --> 14:55.569
This is a comic's manuscript.

14:55.570 --> 14:56.969
Oh, man...

14:55.570 --> 15:00.579
He ignored the art style necessary to make it
in Jump or something, and developed his own!

14:56.970 --> 14:59.879
Mama said
there'd be
days like this.

14:59.880 --> 15:00.880
I'm bored.

15:00.580 --> 15:02.580
No aid to Mars!

15:03.040 --> 15:04.090
- A
- Parsecmen

15:03.040 --> 15:04.089
That's...

15:04.090 --> 15:06.159
Protect article 6000 of the constitution!

15:06.160 --> 15:08.239
No to Martian immigration!

15:08.240 --> 15:10.449
No to criminalizing MILF porn!

15:10.450 --> 15:15.609
Ignoring the will of the people and social
conditions, he constructed his own manifesto.

15:15.610 --> 15:17.559
In a way, he's <i>too</i> proper.

15:17.560 --> 15:25.069
Look, it's the ruins of an ancient civilization which
grew and collapsed while disregarding all others!

15:22.940 --> 15:24.005
Beta

15:24.006 --> 15:25.070
Chibaly Hills

15:25.070 --> 15:30.399
That's just industrial design
that collapsed, ignoring the user's needs!

15:30.400 --> 15:32.319
This must be their ancient currency!

15:32.320 --> 15:37.040
Rather than being influenced by the market like the
yen or the dollar or the euro, it held innate value!

15:37.750 --> 15:40.789
Isn't it better to
go along with the flow just a little bit!?

15:40.790 --> 15:41.500
No.

15:41.780 --> 15:44.679
Miss Kitsu. Were you washed up here too?

15:44.680 --> 15:45.590
Wrong.

15:45.591 --> 15:47.590
I came here of my own will.

15:47.940 --> 15:49.639
I don't go along.

15:49.640 --> 15:51.759
I'd rather
be proper and make up my own mind.

15:51.760 --> 15:54.029
And of course I'd never
be caught up in a mood.

15:54.030 --> 15:55.659
A Sunday afternoon.

15:54.050 --> 16:01.390
Park

15:55.660 --> 15:58.070
The happy lovers and families.

15:57.721 --> 16:01.390
Seurat

15:58.670 --> 16:01.390
That kind
of idyllic, leisurely scene in the park.

16:01.600 --> 16:04.880
But I will not be caught
up in a mood! Saturday!

16:08.350 --> 16:11.910
Come on, there's a difference between not
being caught up and being completely oblivious!

16:11.980 --> 16:16.050
But what of these brave men I've seen
avoiding being caught up in the mood?

16:16.050 --> 16:24.050
※ Pulling a book cart into a fashion-　
able cafe and spreading out doujin
※ Attending the summer and winter festivals
with a baby stroller
※ Wearing panniers on a full train
※ Buying raentzels for other
people's children
※ Going to the bar, drinking nothing
but eating all the snacks
※ Hypermiling and tying up traffic
※ Ignoring the people at the window
and saving one's own department
※ Nioka getting photographed <i>again</i>　　
※ Singing anime theme songs　　　
at people's weddings　　　　

16:17.030 --> 16:19.240
That's just being oblivious!

16:20.480 --> 16:23.089
Everyone's been washed away.

16:23.090 --> 16:24.209
Sekiutsu!

16:24.210 --> 16:25.559
Are you okay!?

16:25.560 --> 16:27.200
You said everyone's been washed away!?

16:27.930 --> 16:29.669
That's okay.

16:29.670 --> 16:31.749
Everyone's so good at it.

16:31.750 --> 16:34.469
I'm sure they're doing
fine no matter where they ended up.

16:34.470 --> 16:38.380
Oh, that's right. It's almost the new
semester, so why don't you bring them all back?

16:39.110 --> 16:41.979
Bring them back? Where are they?

16:41.980 --> 16:46.780
They've washed up
in run-down hostess bars all across Japan!

16:54.780 --> 16:56.870
Soori

16:55.826 --> 16:56.870
Hostess

17:03.660 --> 17:04.940
Welcome.

17:05.300 --> 17:07.170
Haven't seen you around here.

17:07.850 --> 17:08.880
A highball.

17:16.330 --> 17:19.550
A new semester's starting.

17:22.060 --> 17:23.060
Saeko

17:23.020 --> 17:24.309
Harumi?

17:24.310 --> 17:26.640
Yeah, they used to call me that.

17:26.650 --> 17:27.400
- Home Away from Home
- Kaede

17:27.401 --> 17:28.100
- Nami-chan
- Ramen

17:29.720 --> 17:34.520
A new semester's starting.

18:01.470 --> 18:02.930
- Queen of Subtitles
- Queen of Subtitles

18:06.460 --> 18:10.269
Today's the
day we change to summer uniforms!

18:10.270 --> 18:15.359
It might be hard to
notice, but I have summer clothes now too.

18:15.360 --> 18:16.400
By the way...

18:17.240 --> 18:19.220
Uniform
change:
2008/6/1

18:17.740 --> 18:18.690
Your teeth?

18:18.691 --> 18:21.200
The Japanese have a
saying that you can't disguise your teeth.

18:19.221 --> 18:21.200
Don't mention that it's Sunday

18:22.700 --> 18:25.080
But can't their clothing be changed too?

18:25.080 --> 18:25.250
Nowadays, it's good to even have work

18:25.250 --> 18:25.410
-> You've been delaying too long,
don't say you'll do it if you can't.

18:25.410 --> 18:25.580
Everyone supports us.

18:25.580 --> 18:25.750
-> What kind of
company needs to be supported by its fans?

18:25.750 --> 18:25.960
Zetsubou-sensei was pretty interesting

18:25.960 --> 18:26.210
-> If you have time to play around with
this, why aren't you working on Ghostory

18:26.410 --> 18:28.265
Originally published 28th May, Showa 83.

18:26.410 --> 18:30.120
A World of Words

18:28.266 --> 18:30.120
From Chapter 140

18:32.320 --> 18:34.169
What do you mean?

18:34.170 --> 18:35.170
For example.

18:36.290 --> 18:39.300
Putting things in other words.
Doublespeak.

18:38.550 --> 18:39.260
Doublespeak

18:39.260 --> 18:41.300
- ※ Incompatible musical styles (Records didn't sell, we're splitting up the band)
- ※ The DVDs are selling decently We think they'll do good enough. (The sales are lower than last season. If this keeps up it'll get even worse, so there's no way anyone will fund another season.)

18:39.261 --> 18:41.300
- A - A rhetorical trick used to change the impression one's
speech gives. Expressing contradictory positions at once. Example:

18:41.300 --> 18:41.800
- Pyramid
- MLM

18:41.301 --> 18:41.600
New Panties

18:41.320 --> 18:47.539
I propose that we take shocking words and
phrase them in a softer, more summery manner.

18:41.803 --> 18:42.865
Stalker

18:42.010 --> 18:43.475
Arsonist

18:42.866 --> 18:44.540
Shut-in

18:43.220 --> 18:44.720
Housewife

18:43.476 --> 18:45.000
Nouveau

18:44.500 --> 18:45.620
 Comics 　nerd

18:44.721 --> 18:46.370
Panties

18:45.621 --> 18:47.400
Wetback

18:45.680 --> 18:47.270
Ayanami

18:46.270 --> 18:47.560
Normal☆

18:46.850 --> 18:47.850
Overcurious

18:47.540 --> 18:50.939
Like calling a war of
conquest a war on terror!

18:52.540 --> 18:56.089
Or calling getting laid off reclaiming
one's freedom!

18:52.560 --> 18:55.939
Unemployed...

18:55.940 --> 18:57.319
Freedom!

18:57.310 --> 19:01.079
Saying that someone with a funny face
“has character”!

18:57.320 --> 18:59.949
Glug glug

18:59.950 --> 19:01.365
burp

19:01.366 --> 19:02.780
You have charac- ter!

19:02.790 --> 19:02.818
When I was a boy,
and I saw bad anime on TV,
I always wondered what
went wrong and why
they didn't try harder.

19:03.020 --> 19:06.989
They're the same thing, but calling them something
else produces a completely different image!

19:06.990 --> 19:07.800
Yes...

19:07.801 --> 19:10.989
In this season when we change
clothes, we must also reclothe our teeth!

19:10.990 --> 19:17.209
You meen like how we call people who're not
only unemployed, but don't want to work, NEETs?

19:17.210 --> 19:18.839
Well, kind of like that.

19:18.840 --> 19:21.510
You should stop saying such foolish things.

19:21.860 --> 19:22.860
Foolish!?

19:23.090 --> 19:25.639
Foolish. That's
another one of those shocking words.

19:25.640 --> 19:27.470
Why don't we soften it up a bit?

19:28.740 --> 19:30.600
Umm.

19:31.520 --> 19:35.390
An individual
remarkably below-average in reasoning.

19:36.470 --> 19:38.649
What are you
doing making it even more concrete!?

19:38.650 --> 19:40.060
That doesn't soften it at all!

19:41.220 --> 19:46.829
Well, there are lots of situations in which trying
to rephrase something just makes it more obvious.

19:46.830 --> 19:48.319
Like, for example...

19:46.860 --> 19:47.030
A great general
A powerful technique

19:48.320 --> 19:49.469
Nope, not gonna say it.

19:49.470 --> 19:54.170
Wait, doesn't Kafuka
always rephrase things in softer ways?

19:54.170 --> 19:55.170
Ah...

19:56.210 --> 19:58.199
They're not stupid!

19:58.200 --> 20:02.080
They're just people who
are proud of their decision not to think!

20:03.820 --> 20:07.760
That may be true,
but if we just explain it like that...

20:09.590 --> 20:11.719
Looks like it's my turn.

20:11.720 --> 20:12.120
Who's that?

20:12.121 --> 20:15.750
Please, no visitors in the classroom.

20:13.270 --> 20:15.520
- Whoa! Hey there babe, you here to see me?

20:16.560 --> 20:19.089
Don't just go and subtitle me!

20:19.090 --> 20:20.900
Wow, I haven't been called babe in a while.

20:21.210 --> 20:22.499
Teacher!

20:22.500 --> 20:24.699
It's been so long, Kafuka.

20:24.700 --> 20:26.759
Wait, I know her.

20:26.760 --> 20:30.539
She's the famous
movie subtitle translator, Todana Tsuko.

20:30.540 --> 20:32.750
What a-!

20:30.540 --> 20:38.249
She's known for her extremely liberal translations, like
“What a-” for “No!!” and “Write me” for “I love you.”

20:33.010 --> 20:38.250
Write me.

20:38.250 --> 20:40.219
Oh, I see.

20:40.220 --> 20:42.209
I've heard of her, too.

20:42.210 --> 20:47.159
It was impossible not to be moved by her translation of “This
is a hold-up!” as “Don't emit pheromones from your armpits!”

20:47.160 --> 20:51.599
That was very popular.
Especially in Africa.

20:51.600 --> 20:53.179
In Africa!?

20:53.180 --> 20:55.629
You must
be very brave to have made it this far.

20:55.630 --> 21:03.069
Someday I want to call dead bodies on the battlefield
“dreaming natural jelly”, just like Ms. Todana!

21:03.070 --> 21:08.479
I try to make my
translations as fabulous as possible.

21:08.480 --> 21:13.049
Sadly, some of
my viewers just don't seem to understand.

21:13.050 --> 21:18.019
Speaking of which, I really hate being
called “normal”.

21:14.620 --> 21:16.220
Kajiura-speak

21:14.620 --> 21:17.820
Kaida

21:18.020 --> 21:20.420
Can't you think of a better way to put it?

21:21.320 --> 21:23.260
Normal is good enough for normal.

21:24.700 --> 21:26.159
Wait!

21:26.160 --> 21:28.260
C'mon, rephrase it!

21:28.740 --> 21:30.689
No, I think normal
<i>is </i>good enough for normal.

21:30.690 --> 21:31.510
After all, it's normal.

21:31.511 --> 21:33.729
Don't say normal's good enough!

21:33.730 --> 21:35.790
L'Enfant sauvage High

21:33.730 --> 21:37.850
Anyway, let's go into
town and find shocking phrases to soften!

21:39.270 --> 21:41.210
Is this the end for Japan!?

21:41.980 --> 21:44.869
“The end” is a very shocking phrase.

21:44.870 --> 21:46.749
If we don't make it something softer...

21:46.750 --> 21:48.930
Dreams...

21:49.820 --> 21:52.120
Keep the dream alive...

21:53.380 --> 21:57.459
Well, that <i>is</i> a cliche to say after
losses in sports or something...

21:57.460 --> 22:02.169
Yes, people normally
say it rather than saying they've failed.

22:02.170 --> 22:03.300
Excuse me.

22:04.300 --> 22:06.239
Are you happy?

22:06.240 --> 22:08.049
Are you happy?

22:08.050 --> 22:10.930
No matter how you look
at it, that has to be a cult recruiting.

22:11.180 --> 22:14.999
We can't say “cult recruiting” in print.

22:15.000 --> 22:17.410
We've got to find a way to soften it.

22:17.580 --> 22:21.080
“We're practicing how
to tell fortunes. Can we see your palms?”

22:21.080 --> 22:22.080
Cafe New Mombasa

22:21.270 --> 22:22.449
Right?

22:22.450 --> 22:22.980
Exactly.

22:22.981 --> 22:26.900
Well... I guess you can put it like that.

22:27.330 --> 22:31.399
Looking at it that way, everything
in the world can be rephrased.

22:29.136 --> 22:31.370
Tomato Bank

22:31.400 --> 22:36.400
A lot of them,
I don't even have to come up with myself!

22:36.620 --> 22:40.810
In stock

22:36.620 --> 22:38.619
Indeed.

22:38.620 --> 22:43.819
We must produce fabulous
translations, and keep up with society.

22:40.811 --> 22:45.000
Karaoke

22:43.820 --> 22:45.040
That's right.

22:47.240 --> 22:52.449
After all, we call the unemployed who spend
their parents' money at maid cafes “master”.

22:52.450 --> 22:55.589
If we say that students are causing disorder
in class, their guardians will worry.

22:52.470 --> 22:54.030
'Sup, fags

22:54.031 --> 22:55.590
Moron

22:55.590 --> 22:58.119
So we call them “freedom classes” instead.

22:58.120 --> 23:01.059
“Massacre” is too severe of a word for
this.

23:01.060 --> 23:03.729
Let's call it a big Higurashi instead!

23:03.730 --> 23:07.505
Typo

23:03.730 --> 23:06.599
What fabulous translations!

23:06.600 --> 23:09.289
Kafuka truly is fearsome...

23:07.506 --> 23:11.280
Sold out

23:09.290 --> 23:11.280
Fabu... lous, huh.

23:12.660 --> 23:15.049
Just standing here
listening to you all is driving me nuts.

23:15.050 --> 23:18.110
We're changing from winter to
summer uniforms this time, right?

23:23.360 --> 23:25.979
So isn't it weird that we're not
reclothing our teeth more skimpily, too.

23:25.980 --> 23:30.080
Never mind softening things, it'd be
strange if we didn't put them more directly.

23:30.450 --> 23:32.139
Well, that's––

23:32.140 --> 23:35.370
How's everyone doing today!?

23:35.130 --> 23:36.130
SYAMEI
MARU

23:36.131 --> 23:37.130
Shakranger Show

23:37.130 --> 23:40.680
How are all my big boys!?

23:40.270 --> 23:42.600
- Grow up, you creepy nerds.

23:43.480 --> 23:50.900
Shakranger Show

23:43.480 --> 23:46.059
Don't just go and subtitle her!

23:46.060 --> 23:48.379
She wouldn't think that!

23:48.380 --> 23:50.899
But isn't it usually that kind of thing?

23:50.900 --> 23:53.539
Welcome to the kingdom of dreams and hope!

23:51.040 --> 23:53.540
“Welcome to the reality of money and copyright.”

23:53.540 --> 23:55.239
I'm turning in my tickets.

23:53.543 --> 23:55.240
Prize counter

23:53.660 --> 23:55.240
- “Give me cash under the table.”

23:55.240 --> 23:56.249
Miss Kitsu!

23:56.250 --> 23:58.549
If you take
things too far, people will complain!

23:56.891 --> 23:58.540
Squid kebab

23:58.550 --> 24:01.050
Emos can DIAF.

23:58.680 --> 24:01.050
- Thank you for this important advice.

24:02.830 --> 24:04.175
Didoon vs.DGS

24:02.830 --> 24:04.175
Thanks again!

24:02.830 --> 24:04.279
You're such a chicken.

24:04.176 --> 24:05.520
SP Ta♪♪

24:04.176 --> 24:05.520
Moved

24:04.280 --> 24:05.520
Come on...

24:05.880 --> 24:10.590
My expression knows no bounds!

24:10.590 --> 24:10.730
Hero Show

24:10.590 --> 24:10.630
Moe

24:10.630 --> 24:10.730
Mercury

24:10.760 --> 24:12.550
Someone please stop her.

24:10.860 --> 24:12.550
- [Zan] Sayonara Zetsubou-sensei

24:10.860 --> 24:12.550
- Muda tsumo

24:13.930 --> 24:17.100
I'd like to see what
other kinds of comics you can draw.

24:14.090 --> 24:17.100
- This one's getting cancelled.

24:17.390 --> 24:19.149
Am I wrong?

24:19.150 --> 24:21.100
No, I think that one's accurate.

24:21.770 --> 24:25.380
Now I have confidence! I have confidence in
my translations!

24:26.380 --> 24:28.680
Certain viewers have
expressed this opinion.

24:26.480 --> 24:28.680
- Certain viewers are right about us.

24:29.680 --> 24:31.480
Give me religious freedom!

24:29.780 --> 24:31.480
- Give me a church's tax exemption!

24:32.480 --> 24:35.350
In terms of sales, it was a moderate hit.

24:32.620 --> 24:35.350
- Just because it didn't meet expectations doesn't mean it's all bad.

24:36.350 --> 24:38.080
Friendship between Japan and China.

24:36.450 --> 24:38.080
- Give us your money and your tech, Japs.

24:38.490 --> 24:40.619
Stop it, Miss Kitsu!

24:40.620 --> 24:42.060
If you continue being so harsh,

24:42.090 --> 24:44.700
this will end horribly!

24:42.590 --> 24:44.710
- Marry me.

24:50.690 --> 24:51.690
Yes.

24:52.510 --> 24:53.510
Yes!

24:53.900 --> 24:56.979
What a fabulous translation.

24:56.980 --> 24:59.409
In the end, you didn't
have to do anything to it.

24:59.410 --> 25:02.949
Sorry, but I won't let this get any worse.

24:59.560 --> 25:02.950
- Once we get married, let's move in together.

25:02.950 --> 25:05.019
Together forever.

25:03.110 --> 25:05.020
- Someday I will kill you.

25:05.020 --> 25:07.820
Thanks a ton, teach.

25:05.140 --> 25:07.810
- You made a great stepping stone.

25:07.980 --> 25:11.459
But they didn't even
put me in the commercials.

25:11.460 --> 25:13.180
What, you're still blogging? Jesus christ.

25:13.030 --> 25:15.030
The End

25:24.500 --> 25:30.839
Late night, at midnight,
waiting for the night train

25:30.840 --> 25:37.139
Crabwalking on
the cliff-like platform

25:37.140 --> 25:43.429
A life that can fit
into a single suitcase

25:43.430 --> 25:49.810
You, my dear, are
the treasure I chose

25:50.020 --> 25:53.109
As I softly kiss your
closed eyes

25:53.110 --> 25:56.279
The mantle of Hades
will envelop us

25:56.280 --> 26:01.489
You, of all people,
I won't let go on ahead

26:01.490 --> 26:03.489
Let's go on a voyage

26:03.490 --> 26:08.619
Okay, give me your hand

26:08.620 --> 26:14.129
If I'm a slave to my fate,

26:14.130 --> 26:21.259
today's the day I'll
gloriously turn traitor

26:21.260 --> 26:26.980
If death is eternal

26:27.270 --> 26:35.270
Hold on to me, drag me
down, I don't care, let's go

26:36.610 --> 26:44.610
I love you, mon amor

26:44.990 --> 26:47.960
This is a work of fiction. Similarity to any actual zombie serialization, P♪nyo, or Toda Na♪♪♪ko is purely coincidental. PS – No matter how times we sent out an an SOS, we never received support... No. It's all due to the weakness of the production staff. I don't expect you to forgive us. Sorry, Kumeta Koji. Sorry, everyone who's supported us. Thank you so much for everything. Thank you so much for everything. There's just a little bit more.

26:47.980 --> 26:49.690
Despairpiece Theatre

26:49.820 --> 26:52.420
- then Thrice, then Four Times
- The Postman Always Rings Twice,

26:52.420 --> 26:53.420
Ding-dong. Ding-dong.

26:52.423 --> 27:00.423
lleW netsiL

26:53.420 --> 26:54.420
Mail's here!

26:54.420 --> 26:55.420
Ding-dong. Ding-dong.

26:55.421 --> 26:57.880
The mailman always rings
twice, then thrice, then four times.

26:57.881 --> 26:58.899
Come on!

26:58.900 --> 27:03.539
Didn't I tell you to put
it in the mailbox? I sleep in the mornings!

27:03.540 --> 27:04.649
Didn't he hear me?

27:04.650 --> 27:07.929
You've already been privatized,
come on, get it right like they used to.

27:07.930 --> 27:08.939
Ding-dong. Ding-dong.

27:08.940 --> 27:10.069
This is the apartment manager.

27:10.070 --> 27:12.309
The manager always
rings twice, then thrice.

27:12.310 --> 27:16.779
The mailbox is full of your packages,
Kumeta. You should come get them soon.

27:16.780 --> 27:18.569
Ring, ring, ring, ring.

27:18.570 --> 27:20.559
Are you done
yet? Deadline's getting really close.

27:20.560 --> 27:25.269
My editor always rings twice, then thrice, then four
times, then a fifth time. Anyway, I'm the one at fault.

27:25.270 --> 27:30.590
I'm really sorry. I really regret it. A third-rate comicker always
apologizes twice, then thrice, then four times, then a fifth time.

27:30.960 --> 27:35.920
T h a n k y o u !
